course: dictionary
lesson: 15968
title: Unverified: not yet checked
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Verify means to check that something is true. Unverified is the opposite. The prefix un- means not, so unverified means not checked or proved true yet.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The unverified story said the school would close tomorrow.» A story can be true or false, and the word unverified tells us nobody has proved it yet, so we should not believe it straight away.
explain: Scientists use this word too. «The results are unverified, so other teams must repeat the tests.» Unverified does not always mean false. It means the truth is not yet known.
fact: Verified means checked and proved to be true or correct; unverified means not checked yet.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unverified means not verified.
fact: «Unverified reports» are news stories that nobody has checked yet.
fact: Before you share an unverified claim online, check a reliable source.
fact: Unverified does not always mean false; it means the truth is not yet known.
exercise: «The video claims a famous singer has moved to Mars, but it is unverified.» What does unverified mean here? | *Not yet checked or proved true | Proved to be true by experts | Very old | Funny and silly
exercise: Ali sees an unverified post saying his school is closed. What should he do first? | Share it with all his friends straight away | Believe it because it is online | *Check it with a reliable source, such as the school website
exercise: Find and copy the word that shows a claim has not been checked: «The unverified account of the match was posted an hour ago.» | match | posted | account | *unverified
test: «Scientists must repeat the tests because the results are still unverified.» What does still unverified tell us? | The results are very old | The results are very funny | The results are proved and finished | *The results have not been proved yet
test: Which of these is an example of an unverified report? | A weather report proved correct by the Met Office | *A report online that nobody has checked yet | A report from a journalist that three editors have already checked
exam: Which sentence best shows the meaning of unverified? | The story was printed in a long book | *The story has not been checked or proved true yet | The story was checked and proved true | The story was about a very old castle
